blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1893:The statements of this section are not named results of the source article.  They isolate, as exact identities, the register bookkeeping that relates the six-register presentation used in Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary} to the two local extraction blocks $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, and to the register order in which the auxiliary state is already known to be normalized.  Nothing here constructs an extraction isometry, and nothing here proves an approximation estimate: every identity below holds for arbitrary operators and arbitrary vectors, and the only hypotheses that appear are explicit isometry or unitarity equations for the operators involved.
blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1914:	The reference vector on the auxiliary registers $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}' \mid \mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'$ is the strategy state on the two original registers together with one EPR pair on the two first Pauli registers, written in the auxiliary register order.  It is the concrete vector supplied to the residual-distance statement for the auxiliary state of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary}, and it selects no basis vector on either player's original space.
blueprint/src/chapter/ch16_qpbt_extraction.tex:1949:	Write a pair of operators, one on $\mathrm{A}\mathrm{A}'\mathrm{A}''$ and one on $\mathrm{B}\mathrm{B}'\mathrm{B}''$, for their simultaneous placement on the six registers.  Simultaneous placement is multiplicative, commutes with taking adjoints, sends the pair of identities to the identity, and therefore turns conjugation by a pair into conjugation on each block separately.  An arbitrary operator on one player's original register, placed on the six registers, is the placement on that player's block of the operator extended by the identity on that player's two Pauli registers, and the crossed placement of an operator on an extracted register is the placement on that block of the identity tensored with that operator.  Hence conjugating a one-sided placement by a simultaneous placement whose operators satisfy $UU^\dagger = \Id$ on each block only involves the operator of that same side.  Finally, the action of a simultaneous placement is the tensor action of the two block operators after the block reassociation of Definition~\ref{def:extraction-block-order}, it agrees with the tensor action of two linear isometries, and it preserves the norm of every vector as soon as each block operator satisfies $U^\dagger U = \Id$.  These are the placements used in the proof of Lemma~\ref{lem:qld-unitary}; no property of the swap operators of Definition~\ref{def:v-swap-unitary} is assumed here.
